  "track": "track-03",
  "title": "constraints keys defaults identity sequences and computed columns",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "Constraints enforce data invariants at the database boundary, including uniqueness, referential integrity, required values, and domain checks.",
    "Identity and sequence values generate identifiers but do not by themselves guarantee gap-free numbering or business ordering. Their allocation and transaction behavior must be separated from key uniqueness.",
    "Defaults apply when a column value is omitted or DEFAULT is specified; they do not replace NOT NULL or CHECK constraints.",
    "Computed columns derive values from expressions and have persistence and indexability rules. Generated values and constraints should be designed with migrations, concurrency, and application expectations in mind."
  ],
